From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: export the non-coherent DMA cache operations

The T20 soc_vpu driver is built as a module, but it needs the same MIPS
cache maintenance the built-in vendor driver used: its ioctl ABI hands it
a mix of user virtual and physical addresses that only the cache op
helpers can flush by address.

The symbols were arch-internal since the API stopped being exported.
Export them again, GPL-only, with no other change.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/mm/cache.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/cache.c
@@ -79,6 +79,9 @@
 void (*_dma_cache_wback_inv)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
 void (*_dma_cache_wback)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
 void (*_dma_cache_inv)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(_dma_cache_wback_inv);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(_dma_cache_wback);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(_dma_cache_inv);
 
 #endif /* CONFIG_DMA_NONCOHERENT */
 
